              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Matt H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is truly an excellent pie. One minor problem with the recipe keeps it from getting 5 stars: after baking the gingersnap crust, if you just put ice cream right on, the crust starts falling apart. The answer: freeze your baked crust for around an hour and you will be able to put on the other layers with ease. As far as taste goes, this pie is wonderful."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kanada"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe as directed, except I used a 10 inch crust (it wouldn't have fit otherwise). Everyone said they loved it, but I think it was too sweet. Next time I will add half the amount of sugar. I didn't have an issue with my crust falling apart, but I did bake it for 8 minutes and let it cool overnight in the fridge before adding the filling.",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-29T13:50:38.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
